\description{
\code{\link[=fit]{fit()}} and \code{\link[=simulateForest]{simulateForest()}} take their input as a few plain
tables (\code{data.frame} or \code{data.table}), all keyed by an integer site index
\code{siteID} and a \code{year}. This page says what each table must contain, what
may be missing, and what FINN fills in by itself. The bundled Oregon FIA
data (\link{fia_obs_dt}, \link{fia_env_dt}, \link{fia_init_trees}) are a complete example
and the vignette \emph{Preparing your data for FINN}
(\code{vignette("C-Data_preparation", package = "FINN")}) builds them from a raw
tree list.

The short version: build \code{data} and \code{env} with \code{\link[=makeObsData]{makeObsData()}} and
\code{\link[=resolveSiteIDs]{resolveSiteIDs()}}, the initial trees with \code{\link[=makeInitCohorts]{makeInitCohorts()}},
